WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.470
A bus shelter.

2
00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:06.110
A poster: one empty kitchen
chair, and a short headline.

3
00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:10.140
On a phone: an empty park
bench, the same headline,

4
00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:11.770
the same typeface.

5
00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.800
In a magazine: an empty theatre seat.

6
00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:16.550
Then a bus seat.

7
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:17.640
A swing.

8
00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:19.400
A stool at a counter.

9
00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:20.980
Six posters in all.

10
00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:23.610
Six adverts, one campaign.

11
00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:26.550
So is this six texts, or one?

12
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:29.790
In this mission, you'll
learn what a body of work is:

13
00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.920
texts by one creator, studied together.

14
00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:36.510
You'll read an invented
campaign, poster by poster.

15
00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:41.490
And you'll see how one non-literary body
of work can sit in your Individual Oral

16
00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:43.330
beside a literary work.

17
00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:48.350
Your mission: work out how to treat
six adverts as one body of work.
